  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+8a & =18 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot a & =18 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2}-16 & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2} & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=34,$ and $p+q=38.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4)^{2} & =34 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\ |a+4| & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\ a+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{34} \\\\ a & =-4\\pm \\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
